think Designed the eleven double marks as the exact double-line twins at U+2550..U+256C, two parallel rails: horizontal rails on rows 2 and 4, vertical rails on columns 1 and 3, straddling the single-line pen's middle row (3) and column (2). Corners and tees drawn by mirroring/flipping the down-right corner; the cross overlays both double rails.
obs Rota lap (d27), lap-index proxy 1128 logs mod 27 = 21, deep-read ORGANIZING.md -- the placement guide; it confirmed the filing (corpus in image/ its module home, witness in tools/, log in session-logs/, README synced in the same commit per docs-implementation-sync). No churn, no misplacement.
obs Ink band came out 10..20 of 35 as designed -- denser than the light set (4..12) because each line carries two rails; set an honest band 8..22. Compression reported as a fact (encoded 406 > raw 385): like the light box marks the double set is sparse enough that run-length per-run overhead exceeds the raw grid, so the round-trip is the proof, never a false direction-of-compression invariant (avoids the REDS #82 mistake).
